│ The issue arises because the in_bulk() method in the Manager class │
│ is not implemented, and the UniqueConstraint class is missing. The │
│ method is supposed to handle fields that are part of a             │
│ UniqueConstraint by checking if they are unique, but the current   │
│ implementation fails to account for this.                          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                            ✅ Reasoning                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • The in_bulk() method is not implemented in the Manager class,   │
│    leading to the ValueError when called on a field in             │
│    UniqueConstraint.                                               │
│  • The UniqueConstraint class is missing, which is critical for    │
│    Django's constraint system to validate uniqueness.              │
│  • The method should check if the field is unique (via unique=True │
│    or UniqueConstraint) before proceeding with the bulk creation.  │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                 🛠️                                  │
